lit helps users deploy and use linux tools

description:

 lit is a linux tool designed to help with the deployment and usage of other
linux tools. It can either help users through step-by-step instructions or
automated workflows.

modes:

 lit - execution mode, can execute any executable lib file.
 lit-ro - read only mode, can read any lib file.

usage examples:

 lit lit install - install lit system-wide
 lit lit help - print lit help
 lit ssh add-priv-key-temp - add temporary ssh private key
 lit rsync backup snapshot - start rsync snapshot backup

config:

 generated config files for automated workflows will be saved in:

 ~/.config/lib-name/workflow-name.conf

dependecy:

 code dependencies is not recomended, follow this when dependency becomes
 necessarie to avoid code duplication or better code organization.

 all executed script by execution mode will have the env "$APP_PATH"
 filled with current app location full path.

 to import shared dependencies:

  app_path="$APP_PATH"
  source "$app_path/share/shared-script"

 to import local dependencies:

  local_path="$(dirname $(realpath $0))"
  source "$local_path/local-script"

rules:
 1. all code should be human-readable first.
 2. all automated workflow should requires user confirmation before execute.
 3. do not mention this tool name inside other tools code.

directory and files hierarchy:

 README - github standard description file

 bin/ - tool launcher
 bin/lit - execution mode, can execute any executable lib file.
 bin/lit-ro - read only mode, can read any lib file.

 share/ - shared scripts
 share/logger - standard logging

 lib/ - tools library
 lib/lit/ - lit library
 lib/lit/autocomplete
 lib/lit/autocomplete/lit-bash-automcomplete.sh
 lib/lit/install
 lib/lit/help

tools library:

 lib/rsync/
 lib/curl/
 lib/ssh/
 lib/gpg/
 lib/git/
 lib/luks/
 lib/rpm/
 lib/screen/
 lib/docker/
 lib/samba/
 lib/fdisk/
 lib/mount/
 lib/useradd/
 lib/usermod/
 lib/systemd/
 lib/swapfile/
 lib/zram/
 lib/xterm/
 lib/vim/
 lib/openbox/
 lib/pipewire/
 lib/iwd/
